  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve SP&amp;LR for WVs in ASEAN Agri-food</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting decent work for a sustainable, fair, solidarity-based and inclusive development: creating jobs, guaranteeing labor rights, expanding social protection and promoting the social dialogue for all.

In order for marginalized workers in Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam to obtain social protection coverage through Social Protection Floors, they need to become organized so that they can present demands in this regard to their governments either nationally or through ASEAN structures.  For bottom-up implementation of the ASEAN Framework and Action Plan on the Declaration to Strengthen Social Protection, workers in the informal economy in these countries need to be well organised into membership-based organisations of workers in the informal economy, and todevelop the capacity to conduct collective negotiations with national ministries responsible for social protection, including within the context of tripartite structures.

To follow up the workshops on organizing workers in the informal economy which took place in Vietnam and Laos, with participation of members of StreetNet&#x2019;s Cambodia affiliate, IDEA, it is proposed to organize activities which will take this work further.  During the workshops of the previous projects, it was noted that the syndicats of the VGCL have been organizing workers in the informal economy for many years in an isolated way, and they need some exposure to how this is done in other countries beyond the ASEAN region, to broaden their perspective.</narrative>
  </description>
